## Formal signature

`{{predicate-name}} : {{domain}} × {{range}} → Bool`

## Characteristics

- **Functional** — one canonical tool per memorial (OWL 2 RL `prp-fp` surfaces conflicts as queryable)
- **Asymmetric** — A created-with B doesn't imply B created-with A (OWL 2 RL `prp-asyp`)
- **Irreflexive** — a memorial isn't created with itself (OWL 2 RL `prp-irp`)

## When to use created-with

Use `created-with` on every memorial that wants AI-collaboration tool-axis attribution:

- A pair-programmed memoir with both human + LLM tool axes
- An auto-rendered substrate memorial — `created-with sandbar.bootstrap.render`
- A code-generated artifact — `created-with` the generator + the human reviewer
- A migration script's output — `created-with` the migration tool

The substrate carries cardinality-many for flexibility (some memorials are multi-tool), but OWL functional characteristic surfaces conflicts when ambiguity matters.

